Maintainer: Domingos Cardoso <domingoscardoso@jbrj.gov.br>
Description: The 'fungaR' package provides a comprehensive interface to the
    fungal data published by the Flora e Funga do Brasil (FFB) Platform, maintained by the
    Rio de Janeiro Botanical Garden. It offers tools for downloading, parsing,
    and analyzing taxonomic and distributional data published in Darwin Core Archive (DwC-A) format,
    including fungi-specific traits such as nutritional mode, host/substrate, and lichenization status.
    Beyond data retrieval, 'fungaR' also assists taxonomic experts contributing to the FFB
    by simplifying the integration of new fungal species names and records from global mycological
    repositories such as MycoBank, speciesLink, and GBIF.
    The package is designed to streamline both data exploration and data curation workflows,
    integrating seamlessly with the 'tidyverse' for downstream analyses and reproducible
    research pipelines.
